  "rationale": "This invoice from active vendor Gadgets Co. (on file since 2020, contracted Net 30) cannot auto-approve and needs human review, but it is not unpayable. PO-001 alone requires manager approval because the $15,000 total exceeds the $10,000 threshold. IN-003 shows 20 units of GadgetX against standing stock of only 5 (item is active and priced at the catalog $750), so operations must decide whether to accept a backorder or adjust quantity—there is no prior invoice history to treat the overage as routine. TM-003 and TM-001 together flag that the due date equals the invoice date instead of the Net 30 date (~2026-03-01); policy treats on-or-before due dates as a possible coercion tactic, yet the invoice also prints payment_terms Net 30, so a clerk should confirm the intended terms with the buyer/vendor rather than reject outright. Resolve by: (1) manager approval on amount, (2) warehouse/buyer call on the GadgetX quantity vs stock, and (3) confirmation that Net 30 applies and the due-date field is corrected or accepted.",
